  "finding_trace_attribution": {
    "status": "DEFECT (reported, not fixed — business code out of boundary)",
    "summary": "kb-ask produced 2 distinct Langfuse traces for one request: retrieval spans in 16b2b490…, generation + 4 phase spans + 7 scores in b8e36974…. The kb.generation metadata.request_id equals the retrieval trace id (16b2b490…), so unified request_id is present but observations are NOT grouped into one trace.",
    "expected": "one request -> one trace id (hardening item 07 / Q10 evidence ③)",
    "suspected_root_cause": [
      "backend/app/api/routes_kb.py:1032 start_trace('kb-ask') sets _current_trace_id; SSE generator crosses yield boundaries before record_ollama_generation at :1103",
      "backend/app/platform/observability/request_id.py rebinds only _request_id across yields; _current_trace_id (trace.py:33) is not re-bound, so spans.py:79-88 _trace_context() returns None at generation time",
      "backend/app/platform/observability/trace.py:111-120 _open_root calls start_as_current_observation without `with`, so the 'kb-ask' root observation is never ended/flushed (name=kb-ask returns 0 observations)"
    ],
    "reproduce": "POST /api/kb/ask {\"question\":\"什么是检索增强生成？\",\"model\":\"qwen3.8:27b\",\"top_k\":3,\"chunker\":\"v1\"}; then GET /api/public/traces?limit=12&orderBy=timestamp.desc and compare observation traceIds",
